format 1

# Seeded by `pklith seed --init` from the fragments this repository's
# files switch on (`pklith detect`). It is yours now: pklith never rewrites it.
#
# No built-in check reads these types yet, so `pklith check` names them
# until each gets checks or an exempt reason: envrc, gitignore, lock.

## checks
id|category|nix|glob|check|fix|env|msg
# Overrides the catalog row: its globs miss the extension-less hook shims
# pklith seeds into .githooks/ (pklith overrides it the same way).
shellcheck|lint|shellcheck|.githooks/*, .envrc, **/*.sh|shellcheck --shell=bash {{files}}|-|-|shell script finding
# Not in pklith's catalog; ctrm comes from the flake (nix T24), as in
# actlith.
ctrm|lint|-|**/*|ctrm check {{files}}|ctrm fix {{files}}|-|a file holds a character its set does not grant; fix it, or grant it in .ctrm and say why in the commit
# rekall: agent prose and the rules extracted from it (nix T24).
rekall|lint|-|AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, rekall.toml|rekall check|-|-|agent prose drifted from the rules rekall extracted from it; run rekall scan and settle the drift
# xenolith: one language per file (nix T24), as in actlith.
xnl-check|lint|-|**/*.nix, **/*.pkl, .envrc, .githooks/*|xnl check {{files}}|-|-|a host file embeds a non-trivial program in another language; extract it with xnl extract
xnl-lint|lint|-|**/*.nix, **/*.pkl, .envrc, .githooks/*|xnl lint {{files}}|xnl lint --fix {{files}}|-|an embedded or extracted program fails its own language's linter
# The registry judges itself, as in pklith and actlith: generated steps
# match .pklith, and every tracked file type has a row.
gen-check|gate|-|.pklith, hk.pklith.pkl, nix/pklith.nix|pklith gen --check|pklith gen|-|hk.pklith.pkl or nix/pklith.nix no longer matches .pklith; run pklith gen
pklith-check|gate|-|-|pklith check|-|-|a tracked file type has no row in .pklith, a row matches nothing, or a claimed check never reaches its files
doctest|test|cargo|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml|cargo test --doc -q|-|-|a doc example failed
rustdoc|lint|cargo|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml|cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --document-private-items -q|-|RUSTDOCFLAGS=-D warnings|docs do not build cleanly
# Offline, as pklith: advisories need a fetched database, so they are a
# release-time step, not a commit-time one.
deny|supply|cargo-deny|Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, deny.toml|cargo deny check --disable-fetch licenses bans sources|-|-|a license, ban or source rule failed

# xenolith's Rust guards, copied from actlith (nix T26).
rust-mirror|lint|-|**/*.rs, nix/guard/rust-mirror.sh|bash nix/guard/rust-mirror.sh|-|-|a Rust file with logic has no sibling tests.rs wired by #[cfg(test)] mod tests;

# Forge tokens stay out of the library (SPEC.md V2, nix V50).
forge-neutral|lint|-|src/**/*.rs, nix/guard/forge-neutral.sh|bash nix/guard/forge-neutral.sh|-|-|forge-specific text in the library; it belongs in actlith or lablith

# Shared git config stays clean for parallel workers (nix V47).
no-core-worktree|gate|-|-|bash nix/guard/no-core-worktree.sh|-|-|.git/config sets core.worktree, which every worktree shares

tdd-order|coverage|-|**/*.rs, nix/guard/tdd-order.sh, nix/guard/tdd-order.exempt|bash nix/guard/tdd-order.sh|-|-|a commit adds Rust code with no test: commit before it in the push range

test|coverage|cargo-nextest|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock|cargo nextest run --workspace --no-fail-fast --status-level fail --final-status-level fail|-|-|a test failed, or the suite is empty

coverage|coverage|sherd|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, .coverage|sherd coverage --check|-|-|line coverage fell below .coverage

# Generated docs, rendered by pipelith-dev from the files that own their
# facts (dev T18, V40), as actlith-dev does. Each fix is the generator, so
# a commit that changes a source (pklith lay changing hk.pklith.pkl) gets
# the doc rewritten rather than refused.
agents-table|spec|-|hk.pkl, hk.pklith.pkl, AGENTS.md, dev/**|cargo run -q -p pipelith-dev -- agents --check|cargo run -q -p pipelith-dev -- agents|-|AGENTS.md step table is stale
notices|spec|-|Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, docs/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, dev/**|cargo run -q -p pipelith-dev -- notices --check|cargo run -q -p pipelith-dev -- notices|-|docs/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md crate table is stale

## types
type|checks|min|exempt
*|trailing-whitespace, final-newline, line-endings, no-bom, no-merge-conflict, no-case-conflict, no-broken-symlinks, no-private-key, ripsecrets, typos, editorconfig-checker, no-local-paths, ctrm|-|-
editorconfig|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
gitattributes|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
md|markdownlint|-|-
nix|nixfmt, statix, deadnix, xnl-check, xnl-lint|-|-
path:**/SPEC.md|markdownlint, mth-fmt, mth-check, sherd-check, sherd-nav, sherd-budget, itok|-|-
pklith|pklith-check, gen-check, no-core-worktree|-|-
pkl|xnl-check, xnl-lint|-|-
pre-commit|shellcheck, xnl-check, xnl-lint|-|-
pre-push|shellcheck, xnl-check, xnl-lint|-|-
commit-msg|shellcheck, xnl-check, xnl-lint|-|-
envrc|shellcheck, xnl-check, xnl-lint|-|-
sh|shellcheck, shfmt|-|-
toml|taplo|-|-
yaml|yamllint|-|-
gitignore|-|-|git configuration; hygiene steps only
markdownlintignore|-|-|markdownlint configuration; hygiene steps only
path:flake.lock|-|-|written by `nix flake lock`; hygiene steps only
context-limits|itok, sherd-budget|-|-
ctrm|-|-|ctrm configuration; hygiene steps only
ctrm-sets|-|-|ctrm configuration; hygiene steps only
path:AGENTS.md|markdownlint, rekall, agents-table|-|-
path:docs/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md|markdownlint, notices|-|-
path:rekall.toml|taplo, rekall|-|-
path:Cargo.lock|deny|-|-
rs|rustfmt, clippy, rust-mirror, tdd-order, doctest, rustdoc, test, coverage|-|-
# Only the library is held forge-neutral (SPEC.md V2); dev/ (pipelith-dev)
# renders this repository's own GitHub-hosted README badges.
path:src/**/*.rs|rustfmt, clippy, rust-mirror, forge-neutral, tdd-order, doctest, rustdoc, test, coverage|-|-
LICENSE|-|-|license text, nothing to lint
exempt|tdd-order|-|-
yml|yamllint, actionlint, zizmor|-|-
coverage|coverage|-|-
